## 9. Error Handling Strategy

| Error Type | Cause | Response Code | User-Visible Message |
|---|---|---|---|
| `ValidationError` | Invalid input data (e.g., negative amount, missing required field) | 400 Bad Request | "Invalid input data provided. Please check the details and try again." |
| `DependencyError` | Failure in external service (e.g., database unavailable, ML model service down) | 503 Service Unavailable | "The system is temporarily unavailable. Please try again later." |
| `ModelInferenceError` | ML model failed to process input or produced an unexpected result | 500 Internal Server Error | "An error occurred during analysis. Please contact support." |
| `AlertingError` | Failure to create or persist an alert | 500 Internal Server Error | "An error occurred while processing a suspicious transaction. Please contact support." |
| `UnhandledException` | Any other unexpected runtime error | 500 Internal Server Error | "An unexpected error occurred. Please contact support." |

## 10. Test Strategy

**Unit Testing:** Focus on isolating business logic and service components. Mocking dependencies is key.

**Integration Testing:** Verify interactions between components, including database and external services (simulated via Testcontainers).

**End-to-End Testing:** Simulate user interactions and external API calls to validate the complete workflow.

